"""
CRPS Analysis
=============
Continuous Ranked Probability Score (CRPS) on the model-specific bootstrap
predictive distributions used elsewhere in pricing and hedging.

CRPS is a strictly proper scoring rule that jointly rewards point accuracy
AND probabilistic calibration. Lower = better. Same units as the underlying
index (degC for AvgT, degC-days for HDD / CDD / CAT).

For each (model, region, OOS year, month, index type):
  1. Slice the model's 10,000 bootstrap paths to the calendar month.
  2. Aggregate each path to the monthly index value -> empirical predictive
     distribution of the monthly index.
  3. Compute CRPS of that empirical distribution against the realised
     monthly index from region_avg.csv.

Output (booktabs B&W tables, matching Forecast Accuracy_v2 styling):
  99_Thesis Graphs/03_Results/01_Forecast Accuracy/
    csv_crps_raw.csv         — per (model, region, year, month, index)
    csv_crps_by_model.csv    — per (model, index) summary
    T05_crps_AvgT.png        — models x [Mean CRPS, RMSE-equivalent], AvgT
    T05_crps_HDD.png         — same, HDD
    T05_crps_CDD.png         — same, CDD
    T05_crps_CAT.png         — same, CAT

Method note
-----------
For an empirical distribution {x_1, ..., x_n} (sorted ascending) and a
single observation y:

    CRPS = E|X - y| - (1/2) E|X - X'|

The pairwise term has a closed form for sorted samples:

    (1/2) E|X - X'| = (1/n^2) sum_i (2i - n - 1) * x_(i)

Implementation is O(n log n) per cell via a single sort.

Reference: Gneiting & Raftery (2007).
"""

